lagging:
Still dreameth of the bee;
But, tho' the lagging moments pass,
Her Love she may not see.

Radiant and sure, you came a-flying;
Puzzled, you left on lagging feet.
Slow in my breast, my heart is dying.

That I my thoughts may dim;
Haste! lest while you're lagging,
I may remember him!

laggard:
As would let him in--and take him in with tears!" I said.
I lay,--for Love was laggard, O, he came not until dawn,--
I lay and listened for his step and could not get to sleep;

lags:
Those furthest loftiest crags;
Come, Laura, not another maiden lags,
No wilful squirrel wags,
